# API layer

The contract is `src/main/resources/api.yaml`. The OpenAPI generator (`interfaceOnly`, `useSpringBoot3`) emits interfaces in `template.api` and DTOs in `template.api.model`. Change the spec, then implement the generated method. Do not hand-write DTOs or API interfaces.

Controllers are `@RestController` classes that implement the generated interface. They validate HTTP concerns and return `ResponseEntity`. A missing resource is `404`. A conflicting id is `400`.

Business rules that must hold outside HTTP belong in the service. `POST` rejects a client-supplied id in the controller, and `ItemService.create` still throws `ItemIdAlreadySetException` if an id is set.

```java
@Override
public ResponseEntity<ItemDTO> getItem(Long id) {
    return service.get(id).map(this::toDTO).map(ResponseEntity::ok)
            .orElse(ResponseEntity.notFound().build());
}
```

Map only at this boundary: `ItemDTO` ↔ domain `Item`.
